               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 21-year-old male, admitted on 14/09/2009 with a clinical picture consistent with acute appendicitis, presenting with right lower quadrant pain, fever, and elevated inflammatory markers. Physical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient underwent laparoscopic emergency appendectomy without intraoperative complications. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. Analgesia and intravenous fluid replacement were administered throughout the stay. Wound care was performed prior to discharge. The patient was discharged home on 16/09/2009 in good general condition, with instructions regarding wound care and follow-up. Please review the patient in approximately one week. Do not hesitate to contact me should any questions arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
